  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1020 PM CDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nTroughing to our north sends a front south on Thursday. Moisture \nstreaming into the area ahead of the front will cause \nrain/thunderstorm chances to increase Thursday into Friday. Forecast \nsoundings still don't show much of a severe threat with poor lapse \nrates and weak shear at or less than 30 knots. But with forcing from \nthe front, we may have to watch to see if a low strong to severe \nthreat presents itself. Low to medium rain chances will linger this \nweekend with southerly flow and a couple shortwaves tracking through \nthe area. As far as temperatures go, they'll cool some Thursday into \nthe weekend with the breakdown of the high and periods of rain, but \nhighs still look to range from the upper-80s into the low-90s.",
